# INFERRED from live probes on 2026-10-28 (see probes.json). Confirm against .htaccess when the owner provides it.
# Target: Cloudflare Workers static assets `_redirects` file.
# Cloudflare limits (docs page last updated 25 Aug 2026): 2,000 static + 100 dynamic redirects, 1,000 characters per line,
#   statuses 301/302/303/307/308, one splat per rule, query strings cannot be matched, top-most matching rule wins,
#   "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming request",
#   and _redirects does not apply to responses generated by Worker code.
# html_handling (docs page last updated 23 Apr 2026): default auto-trailing-slash. Its own redirects are 307, not 301.
#   Live uses 301 for /path -> /path/, so the 301s are listed explicitly below. They run before html_handling.
#   The "/x /x/ 301" form follows the docs example "/trailing /trailing/ 301". Verify on the preview that it does not loop
#   and that the request query string is passed through (the docs do not say either way).
#   Keep html_handling at "auto-trailing-slash" (or "force-trailing-slash") so /path/ serves /path/index.html with 200.
#
# Lines starting with "# RECOMMENDED:" are NOT live behaviour. They are proposed changes that need owner approval.
# Remove the "# RECOMMENDED: " prefix to enable one. They sit above the live-parity rules on purpose, because the
# top-most matching rule wins.
#
# NOT expressible in _redirects (no host or scheme matching). Configure at the zone, in the Cloudflare dashboard:
#   scheme/http-apex: e.g. http://southfloridasitework.com/ => 301 https://southfloridasitework.com/ -> 200
#   host/http-www: e.g. http://www.southfloridasitework.com/ => 301 https://www.southfloridasitework.com/ -> 301 https://southfloridasitework.com/ -> 200
#   host/https-www: e.g. https://www.southfloridasitework.com/ => 301 https://southfloridasitework.com/ -> 200
#   => Always Use HTTPS (301) for http://, and a Redirect Rule: host www.southfloridasitework.com -> https://southfloridasitework.com/${path} 301, query kept.
#   Live does www and http in separate hops (http://www. is 2 to 3 hops). One hop on Cloudflare is an improvement with the same final URL.
